From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeongwoo Yeom <studavid@cyberperseus.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] configs: j7200: default to eMMC UDA boot

J7200 uses MMC device 0 for eMMC and device 1 for the removable SD card.
Select eMMC UDA partition 2 in the compiled-in environment so systems using
CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE keep booting from eMMC across cold boots and reboots.

Limit standard boot targets to mmc0 to avoid probing the absent SD card if
the TI-specific MMC boot command cannot boot the system.

Signed-off-by: Jeongwoo Yeom <studavid@cyberperseus.com>
---
 board/ti/j721e/j721e.env | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/board/ti/j721e/j721e.env b/board/ti/j721e/j721e.env
index 9e1343a0d9..9bfdbe1d6e 100644
--- a/board/ti/j721e/j721e.env
+++ b/board/ti/j721e/j721e.env
@@ -26,10 +26,10 @@ name_mcur5f0_0fw=/lib/firmware/j7200-mcu-r5f0_0-fw
 name_mcur5f0_0fw=/lib/firmware/j7200-mcu-r5f0_0-fw
 #endif
 
-boot_targets=mmc1 mmc0 usb pxe dhcp
+boot_targets=mmc0
 boot=mmc
-mmcdev=1
-bootpart=1:2
+mmcdev=0
+bootpart=0:2
 bootdir=/boot
 rd_spec=-
 dorprocboot=1
-- 
2.43.0
